      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is straightforward: according to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub never holds the Anthropic API key in its own process environment**. \n\nHere\u0027s how it works:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the child process** \u2014 specifically, into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent process, immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 the key never appears there at all\n\nThis architecture means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables. The key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent as well \u2014 it receives the credential via the same injection mechanism, never through the Hub\u0027s environment.",
